research/twin-council/rounds/r1-codex.log:197:12. **Sell direction, never the digital twin — and never an uncalibrated magnitude.** The literature is consistent: LLM panels get treatment-effect *direction* right (r≈0.85 on copy) but inflate *magnitude*, and individual clones are near-useless (r≈0.20). Every accuracy claim must be scored against the right null ("always predict flat" already scores 67–90% raw) and the product must be positioned as a calibrated prior / triage / bandit warm-start. A bare "+5.0% conversion" before the calibration harness exists is exactly the overclaim a sophisticated buyer (Kohavi) reads as fraud.
